the knowledge base if_example includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/if-example.l4".

the basic whether example is a text if
    the text is equal to "yes"
    otherwise the text is equal to "no".

the check whether positive for a number N is a text if
    N > 0
    and the text is equal to "positive"
    otherwise the text is equal to "not positive".

the absolute value of a number N is a number M if
    N >= 0
    and M is equal to N
    otherwise M = 0 - N.

the letter grade for a score S is a text if
    S >= 90
    and the text is equal to "A"
    otherwise S >= 80
    and the text is equal to "B"
    otherwise S >= 70
    and the text is equal to "C"
    otherwise S >= 60
    and the text is equal to "D"
    otherwise the text is equal to "F".

the can enter venue for an age N with a boolean with a second boolean is a text if
    N >= 21
    and true is equal to the boolean
    or true is equal to the second boolean
    and the text is equal to "Welcome"
    otherwise the text is equal to "Access denied".

a person age P is adult if
    P >= 18.

a number N is adult 2 if
    N >= 18.

the maximum number for a number N with a number M is a value if
    N > M
    and the value is equal to N
    otherwise the value is equal to M.

the list whether true else empty for a condition is a list if
    true is equal to the condition
    and the list is equal to [1, 2, 3]
    otherwise the list is equal to [].

the fibonacci number for a number N is a number M if
    N <= 1
    and M is equal to N
    otherwise a number K = N - 1
    and the fibonacci number for K is a number P
    and a number Q = N - 2
    and the fibonacci number for Q is a number R
    and M = P + R.

L4's answer at line 24 is reproduced if
    the absolute value of 5 is a number N
    and N * 1000000000 >= 4999999999
    and N * 1000000000 <= 5000000001.

L4's answer at line 25 is reproduced if
    the absolute value of -5 is a number N
    and N * 1000000000 >= 4999999999
    and N * 1000000000 <= 5000000001.

L4's answer at line 82 is reproduced if
    the maximum number for 10 with 25 is a value V
    and V * 100000000 >= 2499999999
    and V * 100000000 <= 2500000001.

L4's answer at line 95 is reproduced if
    the fibonacci number for 10 is a number N
    and N * 100000000 >= 5499999999
    and N * 100000000 <= 5500000001.

